<section>
  <h2>Page object pattern</h2>

  <p class="mt-200r fragment">
    Page objects abstract away the technical interactions from the decision code
  </p>

  <if-pw>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      await page.locator('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle').click()  // this is about HTML
    </code></pre>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      await cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();                     // this is about the
                                                                   // application
    </code></pre>
  </if-pw>


  <if-cy>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cy.get('.basket-mini .dropdown-toggle').click()  // this is about HTML
    </code></pre>
    <pre class="fragment"><code class="typescript">
      cataloguePage.displayMiniBasket();               // this is about the
                                                       // application
    </code></pre>
  </if-cy>

</section>

  <!--
  "divide business-oriented decisions, workflows and technical interactions into separate layers."


  |  test layer   |  worfklow component        | technical interaction layer |
  |  - decisions  |  - manipulate page ojects  | -                           |
  |               |                            |



business decision layer:     | test 1 | test 2 | test 3 | ...                  |
worflow layer:               | worflow component 1 | worflow component 2 | ... |
technical interaction layer: | page object 1 | page object 2 | ... | Api client | Api client | ...| 
application:                 | UI                                  | API       |                   |

maybe mermaid's block diagram can help, or simply flex boxes...
-->

<section>

  <table class="fragment mt-200r" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 50%;">
    <tr>
      <td
        style="border: none; width: 250px; text-align: right; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.3rem; vertical-align: middle;">
        Business decision layer</td>
      <td style="border: none; width: 100px; padding: 1em .5em;">
        <div class="flex-row justify-content--flex-start gap-05">
          <div class="rectangle"
            data-arrow="->page-object-1:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'};->page-object-2:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'}">
            test 1</div>
          <div class="rectangle">test 2</div>
          <div class="rectangle">test 3</div>
          <div class="rectangle">…</div>
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: none; text-align: right; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.3rem; vertical-align: middle;">
        Interaction layer</td>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 1em .5em;">
        <div class="flex-row justify-content--flex-start gap-05">
          <div class="rectangle" id="page-object-1"
            data-arrow="->web-page:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'}">
            loginPage</div>
          <div class="rectangle" id="page-object-2"
            data-arrow="->web-page:{'path':'straight','startSocket':'bottom','endSocket':'top'}">productPage</div>
          <div class="rectangle">…</div>
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="border: none; text-align: right; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.3rem; vertical-align: middle;">
        Application</td>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 1em .5em; text-align: center;">
        <img src="img/flaticon_com__webpage_5681787_cropped.png" width="105" style="margin: 0;" id="web-page">
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p class="mt-150 fragment">
    Tests with Page Objects are <strong>easier to read</strong> and
    <strong>easier to maintain</strong>
  </p>
</section>